`RevisionViewer.initialize` receives configuration revisions and selects the record with the greatest revision number. An empty input clears the selection. Revisions must be non-negative integers, and every key and payload must be a non-empty string; any malformed record must throw `TypeError` while leaving the previous selection unchanged. When several records share the greatest revision, retain the first one in input order. The input and its objects must not be mutated. `current()` returns `undefined` when no record is selected and otherwise returns a fresh copy so callers cannot mutate internal state.

